可以。你这四列可以这样理解：

Agent trigger = 用户怎么问时，Agent应该调用这个 function
Controller / Security = 谁有权查、默认限制在哪里
Input = Agent需要传什么参数
Output = 返回给Agent的结构化结果

你可以直接按下面填。

Function	Agent trigger	Controller / Security	Input	Output
searchRequests	Use when the user wants to list or search access requests: “show my pending requests”, “show Sophie’s rejected requests”, “show requests for app X”.	Default scope = authenticated user as requester or requestee. If another userUID is provided, allow only if authenticated user is manager/support/authorized. Default status = pending if not specified.	requesterUID?, requesteeUID?, role?, status?, appName?, entitlementName?, dateRange?, limit?	requestID, requestDate, requesterUID/displayName, requesteeUID/displayName, appName, entitlementName, status, currentStep
getRequestDetails	Use when the user asks details about a specific requestID: “what is the status of request 123?”, “who is the approver?”, “where is it blocked?”.	Allow if authenticated user is requester, requestee, approver, manager of requester/requestee, or authorized support user.	requestID	requestID, requester, requestee, appName, entitlementName, status, currentStep, currentApprover, creationDate, lastUpdateDate, history
getUserAccess	Use when the user wants to know what access a person has: “show my access”, “does Sophie have access to app X?”.	Default = authenticated user. For another userUID, allow only if authenticated user is manager of that user or authorized support/governance user.	userUID?, appName?, entitlementName?, activeOnly?	userUID/displayName, appName, entitlementName, entitlementValue?, accessStatus, assignmentDate?, source?
getTeamAccess	Use when a manager asks for team access: “show my team access”, “who in my team has access to app X?”.	Authenticated user must be manager. Scope limited to direct/authorized team members.	managerUID? default authenticated user, appName?, entitlementName?, activeOnly?	teamMemberUID/displayName, appName, entitlementName, accessStatus, self-report link?
getApplicationOwner	Use when the user asks who owns an application: “who is the owner of app X?”, “who should I contact for app X?”.	Open to internal users if ownership info is already visible internally.	appName	appName, appOwnerUID/displayName, backupOwner?, workgroupName?, contactInfo?
getEntitlementOwner	Use when the user asks who owns an entitlement/role: “who owns entitlement Y?”, “who validates role Z?”.	Open to internal users if ownership info is already visible internally.	entitlementName, appName?	appName, entitlementName, entitlementOwnerUID/displayName, backupOwner?, workgroupName?, contactInfo?
getWorkgroupMembers	Use when the user asks for members/contacts of a workgroup: “who is in workgroup X?”, “who can approve for this workgroup?”.	Open only if workgroup info is visible to internal users; otherwise restrict to authorized support/governance users.	workgroupName	workgroupName, membersUID/displayName, role, email/contactInfo
getUserOwnership	Use when the user asks what a person owns: “what applications does Jean own?”, “which entitlements is Sophie responsible for?”.	Self, manager, support, governance users. Respect visibility of ownership data.	userUID, appName?, entitlementName?	userUID/displayName, ownedApplications, ownedEntitlements, ownedWorkgroups
getPendingApprovals	Use when an approver asks what they need to approve: “what do I need to approve?”, “show my pending approvals”.	Authenticated user must be the approver/validator. Scope limited to their own approval queue.	approverUID? default authenticated user, status=pending, appName?, limit?	requestID, requester, requestee, appName, entitlementName, pendingSince, currentStep, approvalLink?
searchIdentity	Use when the user refers to someone by name and UID is needed for another call: “show Sophie Martin’s access”, “find Jean Dupont”.	Open to internal users, based on Who’s Who visibility. Do not expose confidential attributes.	name, department?, maxResults? default 10	candidateUID, displayName, department, entity, country, managerName
getIdentityDetails	Use when the user asks who someone is or when Agent needs organizational context before another call.	Open to internal users, based on Who’s Who visibility.	UID or displayName	UID, displayName, jobTitle, department, entity, country, managerUID/displayName

